{
  "about": "C5 ground layout, measured by analysis/c5-ground/export_layout.py (PLAN-c5-ground B11). Derived geometry only; regenerate with that script, never edit by hand.",
  "conventions": {
    "uv": "u along the texture's columns, v along its rows, one unit per 256 m repeat; the ground is laid U+X V+Z with whole UVs at world multiples of 256 m on 99.5 % of it",
    "polygons": "flat [u0, v0, u1, v1, ...], convex, counter-clockwise or clockwise; a lot's origin is wrapped into [0, 1) and its polygons are not, so draw each again shifted by -1 and +1 in u and v; a lot's footprint is the union of its polygons",
    "h": "metres from the template ground to the lot's highest vertex over every model it can roll",
    "streets": "the band |c - centre - k| <= half for whole k, c = u, v, u + v or u - v by family",
    "cell": "index floor(c - origin) per family listed; take c from world XZ (u = x / 256, v = z / 256), not from a polygon's own UV, whose origin differs between polygons",
    "sets": "building sets standing on the visible paint, with the world area in km2; none is flagged ground with no layer beneath; on_street is the share of the set's footprint inside the paint's streets"
  },
